  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At Le Brusc, in Six-Fours-les-Plages, Bruscain Paddle rents paddleboards (paddle or motorised) and inflatable kayaks and gives beginner lessons, for two months a year, in July and August. It also offers equipment delivery at Le Brusc (corniche des Îles).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to its website, welcoming dogs is the company's specialty: you can paddle or kayak with your dog. For dog outings, the website mentions suitable paddleboards, life jackets for dogs, a waterproof bag, a bowl, treats and small toys. At Le Brusc, the lagoon is protected (only kayaks, paddleboards and outrigger canoes are allowed, and according to the tourist office swimming is discouraged in the seagrass beds), so check on site whether your dog can swim.</p>

      <h2>Booking and published prices</h2>
      <p>Booking and questions by phone, text or call, on 06 67 30 20 49 (the company's number, given by the website as the easiest way to book). Prices from the "Nos prix" page: paddleboard 18 € per hour, 24 € for 2 hours, 33 € for a half day; paddleboard lessons 45 € per hour, including a lesson "with dog" at the same price; kayak 20 € per hour, 35 € for 2 hours, 40 € for a half day, 50 € for a full day; sunset outing 21 €; motorised water scooter 35 € for 30 minutes. The Provence Méditerranée tourist office (listing updated in June 2025) shows other amounts and an opening period from 1 June to 30 August: the company website's prices, which are more recent, are the ones to rely on; the season announced by the website is July-August. The website also offers equipment delivery at Le Brusc, corniche des Îles.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call before coming to arrange the outing, especially if it's your dog's first time on a paddleboard.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Le Brusc lagoon and the Embiez archipelago are close by.</p>
